{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - MFA - Attempted Bypass of Okta MFA",
	"Description": "Okta recorded an attempt to bypass MFA. Okta emits this when a sign-in tried to get past the factor requirement rather than satisfy it.\n\nEvent type: user.mfa.attempt_bypass\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_attempted_bypass_of_mfa/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_attempted_bypass_of_mfa.yml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
